  "id": "Iran_Signed_a_Ceasefire_Its_Hackers_Didnt_txt_7",
  "content": "Kinetic warfare has rules. Cyberwarfare does not. The Geneva Conventions, drafted in 1949 and refined over the decades that followed, tell us what combatants cannot do to civilians, hospitals, and prisoners of war. They tell us nothing about what a state-aligned hacking group can do to a regional water utility or a prime defense supplier. That gap has become the single most exploited loophole in international conflict.",
